cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "FishCensus"
abstract: >-
  FishCensus is an agent-based model (ABM) that simulates fish assemblages observed during
  underwater visual census (UVC) surveys. The model implements a virtual ecologist approach
  to investigate how fish behaviour — including diver avoidance, attraction, and schooling —
  affects the accuracy and precision of population estimates obtained by different survey
  methods (transects, stationary point counts, and remote cameras). It can be used to
  estimate sampling bias, derive correction factors for field surveys, and guide method
  selection for species with varying behavioural traits.
